      "text": "To find the value of the given expression, we need to apply the difference of squares formula, which is \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\), to each pair of terms within the sum. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **First Pair: \\(19^2 - 17^2\\)**\n   \\[\n   19^2 - 17^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17)\n   \\]\n   Calculate the difference and sum:\n   \\[\n   19 - 17 = 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   19 + 17 = 36\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   19^2 - 17^2 = 2 \\times 36 = 72\n   \\]\n\n2. **Second Pair: \\(15^2 - 13^2\\)**\n   \\[\n   15^2 - 13^2 = (15 - 13)(15 + 13)\n   \\]\n   Calculate the difference and sum:\n   \\[\n   15 - 13 = 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   15 + 13 = 28\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   15^2 - 13^2 = 2 \\times 28 = 56\n   \\]\n\n3. **Third Pair: \\(11^2 - 9^2\\)**\n   \\[\n   11^2 - 9^2 = (11 - 9)(11 + 9)\n   \\]\n   Calculate the difference and sum:\n   \\[\n   11 - 9 = 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   11 + 9 = 20\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   11^2 - 9^2 = 2 \\times 20 = 40\n   \\]\n\n4. **Fourth Pair: \\(7^2 - 5^2\\)**\n   \\[\n   7^2 - 5^2 = (7 - 5)(7 + 5)\n   \\]\n   Calculate the difference and sum:\n   \\[\n   7 - 5 = 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   7 + 5 = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   7^2 - 5^2 = 2 \\times 12 = 24\n   \\]\n\n5. **Fifth Pair: \\(5^2 - 3^2\\)**\n   \\[\n   5^2 - 3^2 = (5 - 3)(5 + 3)\n   \\]\n   Calculate the difference and sum:\n   \\[\n   5 - 3 = 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5 + 3 = 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5^2 - 3^2 = 2 \\times 8 = 16\n   \\]\n\n6. **Sixth Pair: \\(3^2 - 1^2\\)**\n   \\[\n   3^2 - 1^2 = (3 - 1)(3 + 1)\n   \\]\n   Calculate the difference and sum:\n   \\[\n   3 - 1 = 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3 + 1 = 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3^2 - 1^2 = 2 \\times 4 = 8\n   \\]\n\nNow, we add all the results obtained from each pair:\n\n\\[\n72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 16 + 8 = 230\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the given expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{230}\n\\]",
