      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). This will help simplify each grouping of terms in the sequence.\n\nFirst, let's group the terms into pairs that can be factored:\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n1. Identify the sequence components:\n   \\[19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\]\n\n2. Group the terms in pairs:\n   \\[(19^2 - 17^2) + (15^2 - 13^2) + (11^2 - 9^2) + (7^2 - 5^2) + (3^2 - 1^2)\\]\n\n3. Apply the difference of squares formula to each pair:\n   \\[\n   (19^2 - 17^2) = (19 - 17)(19 + 17) = 2 \\times 36 = 72\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (15^2 - 13^2) = (15 - 13)(15 + 13) = 2 \\times 28 = 56\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (11^2 - 9^2) = (11 - 9)(11 + 9) = 2 \\times 20 = 40\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (7^2 - 5^2) = (7 - 5)(7 + 5) = 2 \\times 12 = 24\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (3^2 - 1^2) = (3 - 1)(3 + 1) = 2 \\times 4 = 8\n   \\]\n\n4. Sum the results from each pair:\n   \\[\n   72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 8\n   \\]\n\n5. Calculate the final sum:\n   \\[\n   72 + 56 = 128\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   128 + 40 = 168\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   168 + 24 = 192\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   192 + 8 = 200\n   \\]\n\nFinal Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{200}\n\\]",
