      "text": "To find the value of the sum \\( 19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2 \\), we can use the difference of squares. The difference of squares formula is given by:\n\n\\[\na^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\n\\]\n\nWe apply this formula term by term to simplify the given expression. Let's break it down step by step.\n\n\\[\n19^2 - 17^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17)\n\\]\n\\[\n15^2 - 13^2 = (15 - 13)(15 + 13)\n\\]\n\\[\n11^2 - 9^2 = (11 - 9)(11 + 9)\n\\]\n\\[\n7^2 - 5^2 = (7 - 5)(7 + 5)\n\\]\n\\[\n3^2 - 1^2 = (3 - 1)(3 + 1)\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate each individual term using the difference of squares formula:\n\n\\[\n19 - 17 = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 19 + 17 = 36\n\\]\n\\[\n15 - 13 = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 15 + 13 = 28\n\\]\n\\[\n11 - 9 = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 11 + 9 = 20\n\\]\n\\[\n7 - 5 = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 7 + 5 = 12\n\\]\n\\[\n3 - 1 = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3 + 1 = 4\n\\]\n\nNow we multiply each simplified term:\n\n\\[\n\\text{First part:} \\ (19 - 17)(19 + 17) = 19^2 - 17^2 = 2 \\cdot 36 = 72\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Second part:} \\ (15 - 13)(15 + 13) = 15^2 - 13^2 = 2 \\cdot 28 = 56\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Third part:} \\ (11 - 9)(11 + 9) = 11^2 - 9^2 = 2 \\cdot 20 = 40\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Fourth part:} \\ (7 - 5)(7 + 5) = 7^2 - 5^2 = 2 \\cdot 12 = 24\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Fifth part:} \\ (3 - 1)(3 + 1) = 3^2 - 1^2 = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together gives us:\n\n\\[\n72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 8\n\\]\n\nWe can simply sum these values:\n\n\\[\n72 + 56 = 128\n\\]\n\\[\n128 + 40 = 168\n\\]\n\\[\n168 + 24 = 192\n\\]\n\\[\n192 + 8 = 200\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the equation \\( 19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2 \\) is \\boxed{200}.",
